  "name": "lets-build-a-compiler",
  "description": "A Rust implementation of Jack Crenshaw's 'Let's Build a Compiler' series, targeting x86 assembly generation. The project demonstrates recursive descent parsing, expression translation, control flow structures, and a simple interpreter. It follows a modular structure where different phases of the tutorial (multicharacter tokens, control flow, interpretation) are implemented as distinct modules.",
